# NewTOS native C toolchain — tracking policy.
#
# The ported mintlib libc tree (libc/mintlib with our aarch64 trap-layer +
# newtos-arch glue), the build harness, and the tests ARE tracked: the SDK is a
# self-contained, reproducible LGPL artifact (clone -> build, no external tarball
# dependency). Build artifacts and the not-yet-ported vendored trees are not.

# Build artifacts (regenerable via sdk/libc/build-libc.sh).
# The pristine mintlib source is vendored as sdk/libc/mintlib-0.60.1.tar.xz;
# build-libc.sh extracts it to libc/mintlib/ and overlays sdk/libc/overlay/ —
# that extracted tree is a build artifact, not tracked.
/libc/mintlib/
/libc/build/
/libc/libc.a
/libc/**/*.o
*.NCP

# Vendored trees not yet ported (extracted tarballs, no NewTOS work yet).
# Vendor each when its port begins.
/gemlib/
/cflib/
/apps/

# macOS junk that FAT round-trips create.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.fseventsd
.Trashes
